---
title: "open_obligation - Create Obligation Account (Scallop Lending)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_version_check: check version matches
    q_version_check --> q_create_obligation: version valid
    q_version_check --> q_error: version mismatch
    q_error --> [*]: revert

    q_create_obligation --> q_create_key: obligation = new Obligation()
    q_create_key --> q_create_hotpotato: obligation_key = new ObligationKey(obligation.id)
    q_create_hotpotato --> q_return_tuple: hot_potato = new ObligationHotPotato(obligation.id)
    q_return_tuple --> q_compose_ptb: return (obligation, obligation_key, hot_potato)

    q_compose_ptb --> q_do_actions: execute composable actions (deposit collateral, borrow, etc.)
    q_do_actions --> q_return_obligation: call return_obligation(version, obligation, hot_potato)
    q_return_obligation --> q_share: share_object(obligation)
    q_share --> q_transfer_key: transfer(obligation_key, sender)
    q_transfer_key --> [*]: obligation is shared, key is owned by sender

    note right of q_create_key
        INV-001: obligation_key.obligation_id == obligation.id (key binds to its obligation)
        INV-002: hot_potato must be consumed by return_obligation in same PTB
    end note

    note right of q_share
        INV-003: obligation becomes a shared object (accessible by anyone for deposits)
        INV-004: obligation_key is address-owned (only owner can borrow/withdraw)
        INV-005: each obligation is independent (collateral in one cannot back loans in another)
    end note
